  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); fund balance 617,330 + 561,882 - 528,690 + net transfers 38,272 = 688,794. Transfers printed only as one net line per fund; the governmental total (38,272 net in) is recorded as transfers_in. Business-type from the proprietary statement (p7) Total column, measure net position (modified cash: cash, restricted cash and CDs less customer deposits): 210,996 + 152,477 - 193,766 - 38,272 = 131,435; total expenses 193,766 printed on the Statement of Activities (p2). Proprietary cash flow statement (p8) not recorded (proprietary field is GAAP only; aligned with FY2024). business_type measure stays net position because the recorded figures are the printed Net Position lines (p7). Ending governmental cash = Total assets on the governmental funds balance sheet (all cash, p4); no beginning governmental cash printed. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (totals equal the government-wide governmental column, p1), business-type from p1. Detail: General Fund from the departmental combining statement (p12, General and Recreation columns), which supersedes the General Fund budget schedule (p8, budget figures not mapped to departments: General government 193,902, Park 52,470, Garbage collection 57,631; budget totals resources 233,971, charges 250,350); Street Fund (p9) and Sales Tax Fund (p11) budget schedules; no business-type detail (no utility supplementary schedule; proprietary statement fund columns not added, aligned with FY2024). Other Governmental Fund (Rehab) has no schedule (interest 1, transfers (595)) and is not in detail. Street Fund budget schedule shows capital outlay 18,500 that the fund statement includes in Public works. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
}
